        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left scrotal swelling and associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left side still feels 'bit heavy like full of water'; onset unclear, possibly a few weeks or longer, and patient reports difficulty recalling the timeline. Feels about the same since last visit, with no acute increase in size and no sudden pain. Usually painless; occasional dragging, heavy sensation after a long day working with tools."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated symptom review"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies dysuria, haematuria, urethral discharge, fevers, rigors, nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, and history of sudden severe testicular pain suggestive of torsion."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
