        "code": {
          "text": "General examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well appearing, no acute distress, conversant; slightly vague historian."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Abdominal and inguinal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Abdomen soft and non-tender, no masses. No palpable inguinal hernia with cough impulse."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Current scrotal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left hemiscrotum enlarged, smooth, non-erythematous, skin intact. Left side has a fluctuant, non-tender swelling superior and anterior to the testis; left testis palpated posteriorly with normal size and consistency and no discrete intratesticular solid mass. No warmth, tenderness along the epididymis or cord, or obvious cough impulse. Right testis normal size, shape, and consistency, non-tender; right epididymis and cord normal. No inguinal lymph nodes. Chaperone practice nurse present."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Prior scrotal examination finding"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Transillumination positive over the left swelling at the last visit; not repeated today."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Scrotal ultrasound"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Moderate simple left hydrocele with anechoic fluid around the left testis. Left testis normal size and echotexture, no focal lesion, normal Doppler flow; epididymis unremarkable. Right testis and epididymis normal. No evidence of inguinal hernia or torsion. Report impression: simple left hydrocele; no sonographic evidence of testicular neoplasm."
      }
    },
